<title>USA: U.S. interest rates higher in latest week.</title>
<headline>U.S. interest rates higher in latest week.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve announced average interest rates for the week ended March 21, compared with the March 14 week, as follows:</p>
<p>   Federal funds rate.................5.26 vs 5.19</p>
<p>   3-month Treasury bills.............5.17 vs 5.08</p>
<p>   3-month commercial paper...........5.55 vs 5.46</p>
<p>   3-month bankers acceptances........5.44 vs 5.35</p>
<p>   3-month CDs........................5.54 vs 5.46</p>
<p>   3-month Eurodollar.................5.50 vs 5.44</p>
<p>   30-year Government bond............6.97 vs 6.89</p>
</text>
